<title>BELGIUM: EU says clears BT/Tele Danmark, Swiss telecoms deal.</title>
<headline>EU says clears BT/Tele Danmark, Swiss telecoms deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had cleared a plan by British Telecommunications Plc, Tele Danmark A/S and three Swiss companies to acquire control of Swiss telecoms company Newtelco AG.</p>
<p>The joint venture -- involving Swiss national railway company SBB, supermarket chain Migros and Union Bank of Switzerland -- will operate the second national telecommunications system in Switzerland.</p>
<p>The Commission said in statement IP/97/319 that the venture would have no &quot;significant effect&quot; on competition in Europe. Tele Danmark has a 29 percent stake and BT a 20 percent stake in the group, which was launched last year.</p>
</text>
